By adding 40% towards future prospects and applying the multiplier 17 and deducting 50% of the it towards the personal expenditure of the victim, since the victim was a bachelor at the time of the accident, the Compensation awarded by the Tribunal towards loss of dependency is redetermined as below;
https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 16,000 + 6,400 = 22,400 22,400 x 17 x 12 x  = 22,84,800/-
9.As regards the compensation awarded by the Tribunal under other heads of compensation are concerned, they are just and reasonable and the the same stands confirmed.

